hadiths[132]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The owner of a riding animal has more right to its front part (to sit on)."
"3751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The owner of a riding animal has more right to its front part, except for someone to whom he gives permission."
"3752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angel in charge of the Trumpet has had the Trumpet placed to his mouth since the time he was created, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow into it, so that he may blow."
"3753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything seeks forgiveness for the person of knowledge, even the fish in the sea."
"3754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the morning after Laylat al-Qadr (the Night of Decree), the sun rises without rays, as though it were a basin, until it rises high."
"3755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibn Mas'ud has spoken the truth. Your wife and your children are the most deserving of the charity you give to them."
"3756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever was true to Allah, Allah proved him true."
"3757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth: Your wealth and your children are only a trial. I looked at these two little boys walking and stumbling, and I could not restrain myself until I cut short my speech (the sermon) and picked them up."
"3758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have spoken the truth; the Muslim is the brother of the Muslim."
"3759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity given in secret extinguishes the anger of the Lord."
"3760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity given in secret extinguishes the anger of the Lord, maintaining ties of kinship increases one's lifespan, and doing good protects against an evil death."
"3761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sadaqat al-Fitr is one sa' of dates, or one sa' of barley, or two mudds of wheat, on behalf of every young and old, free and slave."
"3762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is a charity which Allah has bestowed upon you, so accept His charity."
"3763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity given by a relative to a relative is both charity and the maintaining of kinship ties."
"3764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your young children (who die) are the little creatures of Paradise. One of them will meet his father and take hold of his garment, and he will not let go until Allah admits him and his father into Paradise."
"3765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah's chosen land on His earth is Sham (Greater Syria), and in it are His chosen ones from among His creation and His servants. And a group from my Ummah will surely enter Paradise with neither reckoning nor punishment upon them."
"3766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Maintaining ties of kinship increases one's lifespan, and charity given in secret extinguishes the anger of the Lord."
"3767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Maintaining ties of kinship, good character and being a good neighbour: these make homes flourish and increase lifespans."
"3768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Maintaining ties with relatives is a cause of increase in wealth, of love within the family, and of delay in one's appointed time (an increase in lifespan)."
"3769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep ties with whoever cuts you off, do good to whoever does evil to you, and speak the truth even if it is against yourself."
"3770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray the prayer at its proper time. Then, if you find the imam leading the people in prayer, pray with them (as well). Your (first) prayer has already been secured for you, and otherwise this (second prayer) will be a voluntary prayer for you."
"3771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray the prayer at its proper time. Then, if you find them (praying), pray with them (as well), and do not say, 'I have already prayed, so I will not pray (again).'"
"3772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In prayer, recite 'Wash-shamsi wa duhaha' (By the sun and its morning brightness) and surahs like it."
"3773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Lead the prayer in a manner (as light as) the weakest person can bear, and do not appoint a mu'adhdhin who takes a wage for his adhan."
"3774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray two rak'ahs and keep them short. And when one of you comes on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him pray two rak'ahs and keep them light."
"3775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray the Fajr prayer, then refrain from prayer until the sun has risen and become high, for when it rises it rises between the two horns of Satan, and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it. Then pray, for the prayer at that time is witnessed and attended (by the angels), until the shadow becomes equal to the spear. Then refrain from prayer, for at that time Hell is stoked. Then, when the shadow begins to lengthen (after the zenith), pray, for the prayer at that time is also witnessed and attended (by the angels), until you pray Asr. Then refrain from prayer until the sun sets, for when it sets it sets between the two horns of Satan, and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it."
"3776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray as someone bidding farewell would pray, as though you see Him; and if you do not see Him, then He sees you. Despair of what is in the hands of people, and you will live free of need. And beware of anything for which you would have to apologise."
"3777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray standing, unless you fear drowning."
"3778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray standing; if you are not able, then sitting; and if you cannot do even that, then lying on your side."
"3779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people, pray in your homes, for the best prayer is a man's prayer in his home, except for the obligatory prayer."
"3780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray the Maghrib prayer as soon as the sun sets; hasten to it before the stars appear."
"3781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you mention me, send blessings upon the prophets as well, for they were sent just as I was sent."
"3782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Send blessings upon the prophets and messengers of Allah, for Allah sent them just as He sent me."
"3783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Send blessings upon me and strive hard in supplication, and say: 'Allahumma salli ala Muhammadin wa ala ali Muhammad, wa barik ala Muhammadin wa ali Muhammad, kama barakta ala Ibrahima wa ali Ibrahim, innaka Hamidun Majid' (O Allah, send Your mercy upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and send Your blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious)."
"3784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in your homes, and do not turn them into graves."
"3785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in your homes, and do not turn them into graves. Do not make my house (grave) a place of festivity. Send blessings and peace upon me, for your blessings reach me wherever you may be."
"3786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in your homes, and do not abandon voluntary prayers in them."
"3787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in the sheepfolds, and do not pray in the resting places of camels."
"3788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in the sheepfolds, and do not pray in the resting places of camels, for they were created from devils."
"3789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in the sheepfold and wipe their noses (treat them kindly), for they are among the animals of Paradise."
"3790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray in your shoes, and do not imitate the Jews."
"3791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib. Pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib, for whoever wishes (to pray them)."
"3792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you wish to enter the House (the Ka'bah), pray in the Hijr (of Isma'il), for it is part of the House. But when your people built the Ka'bah, they shortened it and left it out of the House."
"3793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Observe the best fasting, and that is the fasting of Dawud (peace be upon him): fasting one day and not fasting the next."
"3794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast the month of patience, Ramadan. Fast the month of patience, and three days of every month."
"3795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Acts of kindness protect against evil deaths, calamities and destruction, and those who do good in this world will be the people of goodness (counted among them) in the Hereafter as well."
"3796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Acts of kindness protect against evil deaths, secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, maintaining ties of kinship increases one's lifespan, and every good deed is charity. Those who do good in this world will be the people of goodness in the Hereafter as well, and those who do evil in this world will be the people of evil in the Hereafter as well."
"3797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Acts of kindness protect against evil deaths, secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, and maintaining ties of kinship increases one's lifespan."
"3798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two kinds of people from my Ummah will never be reached by my intercession: an oppressive, tyrannical ruler, and every extremist who has departed from the religion."
"3799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two kinds of the people of Hell whom I have not yet seen: people who have whips like the tails of cattle with which they beat people, and women who are clothed yet naked, who incline others (to evil) and are themselves inclined, their heads like the leaning humps of Bactrian camels. These women will not enter Paradise nor find its fragrance, although its fragrance can be perceived from such and such a distance."
"3800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a thousand men."
"3801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two sounds are cursed in this world and the Hereafter: playing a musical pipe (instrument) at a time of joy, and wailing and lamenting (mourning) at a time of calamity."
"3802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days of every month, and fasting from one Ramadan to the next Ramadan, is equal to fasting perpetually and breaking the fast (in between)."
"3803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting the month of patience and fasting three days of every month is equal to fasting perpetually."
"3804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting the month of patience and fasting three days of every month removes the heat (rancour) of the chest."
"3805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting the day of Arafah is a means of expiation for (the sins of) the past year and the coming year."
"3806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting the day of Arafah expiates the sins of two years, the past and the coming, and fasting the day of Ashura expiates the sins of one past year."
"3807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your day of fasting is the day on which you (all) fast, and your day of sacrifice is the day on which you (all) offer sacrifice."
"3808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast the month, and also its last dark nights."
"3809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast upon sighting the moon and stop fasting upon sighting the moon. If clouds come between you and the moon, then complete the count of Sha'ban. Do not go out to welcome the month (of Ramadan) in advance, and do not join a day of Sha'ban to Ramadan."
"3810","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast upon sighting the moon and stop fasting upon sighting the moon, and if (the moon) is hidden from you, then complete thirty days of Sha'ban."
"3811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast upon sighting the moon, stop fasting upon sighting the moon, and offer your sacrifices according to it. If (the moon) is hidden from you, then complete thirty days, and if two Muslim witnesses testify, then fast and stop fasting (accordingly)."
"3812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast from one brightness (of the moon/day) to the next brightness (of the moon/day)."
"3813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast on behalf of your sister."
"3814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of any one of you in his house is better than his prayer in this mosque of mine, except for the obligatory prayer."
"3815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of the Awwabin (the forenoon prayer) is when the young camels begin to feel the heat (of the sun)."
"3816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of one who sits carries half (the reward) of the prayer of one who stands."
"3817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer in congregation is twenty-five times more excellent than the prayer of any one of you performed alone."
"3818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer in congregation is equal to twenty-five times the prayer performed alone."
"3819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer in congregation is twenty-five degrees more excellent than the prayer performed alone."
"3820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer in congregation is twenty-seven degrees more excellent than the prayer performed alone."
"3821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's voluntary prayer where people do not see him is equal to twenty-five times the prayer performed before the eyes of people."
"3822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer performed alone by twenty-five degrees."
"3823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer in his house and his prayer in his marketplace by twenty-five degrees. That is because when one of you performs ablution and does it well, then comes to the mosque intending nothing but the prayer, he does not take a single step except that Allah raises him a degree by it and forgives him a sin by it, until he enters the mosque. Then, when he enters the mosque, he is counted as being in prayer as long as the prayer keeps him there, and the angels continue to supplicate for him as long as he remains seated in the place where he prayed, saying: O Allah, forgive him! O Allah, have mercy on him! O Allah, accept his repentance! as long as he does not harm anyone there or break his ablution."
"3824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer performed alone by twenty-five degrees, and if he prays in a desolate place and completes its ablution, its bowing and its prostrations, his prayer reaches fifty degrees."
"3825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer standing is better than his prayer sitting, his prayer sitting carries half (the reward) of his prayer standing, and his prayer lying down carries half (the reward) of his prayer sitting."
"3826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer while sitting is (equal to) half a prayer, but I am not like any one of you."
"3827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The forenoon prayer is the prayer of the Awwabin."
"3828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of one who sits carries half (the reward) of the prayer of one who stands."
"3829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The night prayer is two units at a time. So when any one of you fears the arrival of dawn, let him pray one unit; it will make what he has already prayed odd (witr)."
"3830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The night prayer is two units at a time, and the witr is one unit in the last part of the night."
"3831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The (voluntary) prayer of the night and the day is two units at a time."
"3833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman's praying in her house is better than her praying in her courtyard room, and her praying in her inner chamber is better than her praying in her house."
"3834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the day."
"3835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"3836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of two men, one of whom leads the other, is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of four men praying separately (one after another). The prayer of four men led by one of them is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of eight men praying separately, and the prayer of eight men led by one of them is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of a hundred men praying separately."
"3837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A prayer following another prayer, with no idle talk between them, is recorded in Illiyyin."
"3838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A single prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in all other mosques except al-Masjid al-Haram, and a single prayer in al-Masjid al-Haram is better than a hundred thousand prayers in all other mosques."
"3839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A single prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in all other mosques except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"3840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A single prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in all other mosques except al-Masjid al-Haram, for I am the last of the Prophets and my mosque is the last of the mosques."
"3841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A single prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in all other mosques except al-Masjid al-Haram, and a single prayer in al-Masjid al-Haram is better than a prayer in this mosque of mine by a hundred prayers."
"3842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Praying with the imam is better than twenty-five prayers that one prays alone."
"3843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two prayers after which no prayer is offered: after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and after the Asr prayer until the sun sets."
"3844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your (O women!) praying in your houses is better than your praying in your rooms, your praying in your rooms is better than your praying in your compounds (courtyards), and your praying in your compounds is better than praying in the congregational mosque."
"3845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The early people of this Ummah were reformed through abstinence and certainty, and its last people will be destroyed through miserliness and (long) hopes."
"3846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The crying of a newborn child (at the time of birth) is due to a prod (jab) of Satan."
"3847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person's fasting in the path of Allah removes him from Hell by the distance of a seventy-year journey."
"3848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days of every month is equal to fasting perpetually, and to breaking the fast as well."
"3849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days of every month is equal to fasting perpetually, and they are the White Days: the mornings of the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."
"3850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days in the month is a good fast."
"3851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting the month of Ramadan is equal to ten months of fasting, and fasting six days after it is equal to two months, so this becomes equal to fasting the whole year."
"3852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting on Saturday is neither for you nor against you."
"3853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting on the day of Arafah: I hope that through it Allah will forgive the sins of the year before it and the year after it. And fasting on the day of Ashura: I hope that through it Allah will forgive the sins of the year before it."
"3854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One who observes a voluntary fast is in charge of himself: if he wishes he may complete the fast, and if he wishes he may break it."
"3855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The truly patient one is he who is patient at the time of the first shock."
"3856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The true place of patience is at the time of the first shock."
"3857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Patience is at the time of the first shock."
"3858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Giving charity to a needy person is only charity, but giving charity to a relative is two things: charity and also maintaining the ties of kinship."
"3859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The true wrestler is the one who becomes angry, and his anger becomes intense, his face turns red and his hair stands on end, yet he still throws down his anger."
"3860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pure earth is the ablution (wudu) of a Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years."
"3861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Earth is the ablution (wudu) of a Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years. Then when he finds water, he should fear Allah and let it touch his skin, for that is better."
"3862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Reconciliation between Muslims is permissible, except a reconciliation that makes something unlawful lawful or makes something lawful unlawful."
"3863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Trumpet is a horn into which it will be blown."
"3864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The essence of an image is the head, so when the head is cut off, no image remains."
"3865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield."
"3866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield for protection from the punishment of Allah."
"3867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield through which the servant gains protection from Hell."
"3868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting in winter is a cool booty (that is, one gained without hardship)."
"3869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fast is on the day you all fast, and Eid al-Fitr is on the day you all break the fast, and Eid al-Adha is on the day you all offer sacrifice."
"3870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer is the best thing that has been prescribed, so whoever is able to offer as many voluntary prayers as possible, let him offer many."
"3871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer in congregation is equal to twenty-five prayers, and if he offers it in an open wilderness and completes its bowing and prostration, it reaches the equal of fifty prayers."
"3872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Praying in the Masjid of Quba is equal to an Umrah."
"3873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take care of the prayer! And take care of those whom you own! Take care of the prayer! And take care of those whom you own!"
"3874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The five prayers are an expiation for (the sins committed) between them, provided that major sins are avoided, and from one Friday to the next Friday and three additional days (are also an expiation)."
"3875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The five prayers, from one Friday to the next Friday, and from one Ramadan to the next Ramadan, are an expiation for the sins committed between them, provided that major sins are avoided."
"3876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield."
"3877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield. When one of you is fasting, he should neither speak obscenely nor act ignorantly, and if a man fights him or abuses him, he should say twice: 'I am fasting.' By the One in whose Hand is my soul! The smell of the fasting person's mouth is better with Allah than the fragrance of musk. He gives up his food, his drink and his desire for My sake; fasting is for Me and I Myself will reward it, and a good deed is recorded as ten times its like."
"3878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield from the Fire (for protection), so whoever begins the morning fasting should not act ignorantly that day, and if a man acts ignorantly towards him, he should neither abuse him nor revile him, but should say: 'I am fasting.' By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! The smell of the fasting person's mouth is better with Allah than the fragrance of musk."
"3879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield from the Fire (for protection), just like the shield one of you has for protection in battle."
"3880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield and a strong fortress for protection from the Fire."
"3881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield and it is one of the fortresses of the believer. The reward of every deed is for the one who does it, except fasting. Allah says: 'Fasting is for Me and I Myself will reward it.'"
"3882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting and the Qur'an will intercede for the servant on the Day of Resurrection. Fasting will say: 'O Lord! I kept him from food, drink and desires during the day, so accept my intercession for him.' And the Qur'an will say: 'O Lord! I kept him from sleep at night, so accept my intercession for him.' So the intercession of both will be accepted."
